Fonts
-----

The web and desktop builds embed two typefaces, taken unmodified from the
`epaint_default_fonts` crate rather than vendored here, so the upstream licence
files travel with the dependency. They are redistributed in the compiled
binary, which is what makes these notices obligations.

  Ubuntu Light — Ubuntu Font Licence 1.0, Copyright 2010,2011 Canonical Ltd.
    Used for all proportional text. Unmodified; no derivative is produced, so
    the licence's renaming requirement does not arise.

  Hack Regular — MIT, Copyright 2018 Source Foundry Authors; derived from
    DejaVu (public domain) and Bitstream Vera Sans Mono, Copyright 2003
    Bitstream Inc., Bitstream Vera Licence with Reserved Font Names
    "Bitstream" and "Vera". Used for type names and any monospaced text.
    Unmodified.

Full texts ship with the crate, as `fonts/UFL.txt` and `fonts/Hack-Regular.txt`
under `epaint_default_fonts`. egui's two bundled emoji faces are deliberately
not registered — see docs/architecture.md D4.

A third typeface is vendored in this repository, because it is registered only
when a schema needs it and so cannot come from a crate that is compiled in
unconditionally:

  Noto Sans CJK TC Regular — SIL Open Font Licence 1.1, Copyright 2014-2021
    Adobe (github.com/adobe-fonts/source-han-sans), with Reserved Font Name
    "Source". Used for Han, kana, Hangul and Bopomofo text in schemas and
    comments. Unmodified.

  crates/view/assets/NotoSansCJKtc-Regular.otf
  crates/view/assets/NotoSansCJK-LICENSE.txt  — the full OFL 1.1 text

The web build serves the file rather than compiling it in, so it is
redistributed both ways; the licence file above is copied into `dist/` alongside
it.


